From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] linux: capture the tag_8021q DSA taggers as standard Ethernet

libpcap gives a DSA conduit with a tagger it does not know a debug-only
link type, as such a tagger usually inserts its own header. The
qca-8021q, rtl8365mb-8021q and an8855-8021q taggers do not: they put
only a standard 802.1Q header on the conduit and identify the port by
its VID. Treat them like a conduit without a tagger, so Ethernet
decoding and VLAN filtering keep working.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/pcap-linux.c
+++ b/pcap-linux.c
@@ -5776,7 +5776,14 @@ iface_dsa_get_proto_info(const char *dev
 	 * any tagging protocol configured, and is therefore a standard
 	 * Ethernet interface.
 	 */
-	if (strcmp(buf, "none") == 0)
+	/*
+	 * The tag_8021q taggers below put only a standard 802.1Q header on
+	 * the conduit, so it is a standard Ethernet interface as well.
+	 */
+	if (strcmp(buf, "none") == 0 ||
+	    strcmp(buf, "qca-8021q") == 0 ||
+	    strcmp(buf, "rtl8365mb-8021q") == 0 ||
+	    strcmp(buf, "an8855-8021q") == 0)
 		return 0;
 
 	/*
